<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 251 0 R
/E (Student alcohol and substance use perceptions are shaped by social environments, norms, and culture. Decisions around use are influenced by stress, peers, and access. While harm reduction strategies exist, they are often inconsistently used, or limited by stigma and a lack of practical education. Our findings highlight the need to shift both institutional and peer norms to better support safety around polysubstance use among UNC students.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
